<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Trubadur on Typophile Archive</title><link>https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/tags/trubadur/</link><description>Recent content in Trubadur on Typophile Archive</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Wed, 13 Jan 2010 01:15:00 +0100</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/tags/trubadur/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Trubadur Released</title><link>https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/66173/</link><pubDate>Wed, 13 Jan 2010 01:15:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/66173/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Sweet noble heart, pretty lady,&lt;br&gt;
I am wounded by love&lt;br&gt;
so that I am sad and pensive,&lt;br&gt;
and have no joy or mirth,&lt;br&gt;
for to you, my sweet companion,&lt;br&gt;
I have thus given my heart.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;P.S. - Take this font as a part of my heart.&lt;/p&gt;
